WEBVTT

00:03.750 --> 00:06.290
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

00:07.380 --> 00:12.750
Spanning more than 400 years since
the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

00:07.920 --> 00:10.880
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

00:17.130 --> 00:20.750
<b>Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto - Elda</b>

00:27.170 --> 00:29.080
Has the time finally come?

00:30.170 --> 00:33.750
The days have been so long
it feels like an eternity has passed.

00:35.460 --> 00:36.790
I have so longed for this!

00:37.830 --> 00:40.250
The pudding I've been waiting five months for
is on it's way!

00:40.460 --> 00:43.040
<b>"Potato Honey Kintoki Mousse Pudding" shipping confirmation notice</b>

00:43.460 --> 00:47.630
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

00:48.130 --> 00:50.460
was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

00:51.380 --> 00:55.040
Hurry up, hurry up, delivery person!

02:27.170 --> 02:31.880
<b>EPISODE 3</b>

02:27.170 --> 02:31.880
<b>THE NEW PRIESTESS AND</b>

02:27.170 --> 02:31.880
<b>THE RITUAL OF SUCCESSION</b>

02:29.580 --> 02:33.500
Ah, I'm finally done. Sorry I made you wait, Koito.

02:33.580 --> 02:38.500
Nice work, Koma-chan. Being a committee member
for the cultural festival is surprisingly hard.

02:38.710 --> 02:42.830
I became a candidate because it looked like fun,
but now it's just a pain.

02:44.080 --> 02:45.250
Hang in there.

02:45.500 --> 02:46.960
What're you reading?

02:47.330 --> 02:48.500
A gift catalog.

02:49.380 --> 02:55.630
A parishioner who moved to Nagano sent us apples.
Grandpa left choosing the return gift to me.

02:56.250 --> 03:00.130
Since they went to all the trouble,
I'm thinking of ordering something nice to send back.

03:00.500 --> 03:03.670
I'm so stumped on what I should give them, though.

03:04.170 --> 03:07.500
Can't you play it safe
and send them a cake or something?

03:09.790 --> 03:14.000
If it were me, I'd want meat. Really good meat.

03:15.540 --> 03:18.420
Oh, meat's a good one. Meat is great.

03:18.960 --> 03:21.250
Look at this meat, it looks awesome.

03:21.830 --> 03:23.830
Whoa, for real. Looks delicious.

03:24.380 --> 03:26.250
Mail order food is great.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.130
Yeah, it is.

03:29.710 --> 03:33.080
Koganei-sama, Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama!

03:33.500 --> 03:34.960
Delivery!

03:39.210 --> 03:40.290
Stamp, please!

03:43.000 --> 03:44.920
Th-thank you.

03:52.670 --> 03:54.080
It's finally here!

03:54.790 --> 03:59.750
It's been number one on the ranking charts
for 3 years straight! And it sells out every day!

04:00.000 --> 04:02.420
Sweet potato honey and red bean mousse pudding!

04:03.040 --> 04:06.080
The reviews were good, so that's very promising!

04:06.290 --> 04:07.750
I'll make more tea.

04:11.290 --> 04:14.170
It's about time for Koito to get home.

04:15.460 --> 04:17.380
Maybe we can eat this together.

04:17.790 --> 04:25.630
<b>Alone</b>

04:17.790 --> 04:25.630
<b>Together</b>

04:17.920 --> 04:23.500
W-well, but I reserved this pudding forever ago,
and I was finally able to order one...

04:23.670 --> 04:25.630
I-it's okay if I eat it all myself!

04:25.790 --> 04:27.000
I'm back, Elda.

04:30.210 --> 04:32.670
W-welcome home.

04:36.290 --> 04:37.540
Did we get a delivery?

04:37.880 --> 04:40.580
N-no... Yes, kind of...

04:41.210 --> 04:44.460
What do you need? There's no shrine ritual today, right?

04:44.710 --> 04:47.080
I bought some ice cream. Let's eat them together.

04:47.080 --> 04:47.830
Huh?

04:48.330 --> 04:52.630
Koma-chan told me about this.
It's ice cream exclusive to convenience stores in Tokyo.

04:53.170 --> 04:55.630
<b>TOKYO MILK ICE CREAM</b>

04:53.250 --> 04:55.540
Elda, you like exclusive items, right?

04:58.130 --> 05:03.380
I'm sorry! I'm a despicable elf who tried to keep these
all for myself and I'm sorry!

05:03.750 --> 05:04.380
What?!

05:09.630 --> 05:13.420
Yummy! It's like they only
gathered honey from the potato!

05:14.130 --> 05:17.750
Yes. I'm ever so pleased you enjoy it.

05:17.880 --> 05:19.330
Why are you talking like that?!

05:19.710 --> 05:23.330
C'mon, that's enough! Have some, too, Elda!

05:23.330 --> 05:24.130
Okay!

05:27.080 --> 05:31.920
Delicious... it's delicious. Truly a special order.

05:32.210 --> 05:35.330
<b>POTATO HONEY</b>

05:32.210 --> 05:35.330
<b>KINTOKI MOUSSE</b>

05:32.210 --> 05:35.330
<b>PUDDING</b>

05:32.670 --> 05:35.170
And the last one is for Koyuzu.

05:35.580 --> 05:39.920
Speaking of, earlier I was talking about
the mail order food with Koma-chan.

05:40.290 --> 05:42.710
Matsusaka beef looks so good.

05:43.080 --> 05:44.380
Mail order, huh...?

05:45.170 --> 05:49.380
It's amazing you can enjoy mail order foods
no matter the area or the season.

05:49.380 --> 05:51.880
Yeah! Thanks to delivery people.

05:52.250 --> 05:55.380
And then there's the refrigeration
and freezing technology...

05:56.000 --> 05:58.250
Those didn't exist back in the Edo days,

05:58.710 --> 06:02.790
so something out of season like ice in the summer
was a very valuable thing.

06:03.040 --> 06:05.670
If it was valuable, then it was there for a reason, right?

06:06.130 --> 06:09.040
We cut out the ice that we made during winter.

06:09.420 --> 06:14.580
It was kept in storage facility called an "cold room"
that was made deep in the mountainside and in caves.

06:11.130 --> 06:17.380
<b>Cold Room</b>

06:14.960 --> 06:17.210
Wow, a natural refrigerator.

06:17.380 --> 06:18.710
<b>KAGA</b>

06:17.880 --> 06:21.170
In Edo, we called ice in the summer "Blessed Ice."

06:21.500 --> 06:24.250
Every year on June 1st of lunar calendar,

06:24.420 --> 06:28.040
ice from the cold rooms in Kaga Province
was delivered to the Edo shogunate.

06:27.750 --> 06:29.000
<b>EDO</b>

06:29.170 --> 06:31.710
Did the shogun eat shaved ice and stuff?

06:32.000 --> 06:38.500
No, it wasn't fit for consumption, so they'd touch it to cool
themselves down and chill fruit and things of that sort.

06:38.830 --> 06:44.290
I was so happy to have
even just a little bit of Blessed Ice...

06:45.460 --> 06:46.960
What did you use it for, Elda?

06:46.960 --> 06:54.670
<b>O-oh no,</b>

06:46.960 --> 06:54.670
<b>my stomach is...?</b>

06:47.710 --> 06:49.500
I ate it and upset my stomach.

06:49.630 --> 06:51.420
You said yourself it wasn't fit for consumption.

06:51.670 --> 06:54.250
I just got so excited, I couldn't help it.

06:55.420 --> 06:58.630
Aww, we ate it all.

06:59.960 --> 07:02.040
It was ridiculously delicious.

07:02.380 --> 07:07.380
Yeah, and from here on let's call mail order food
"Blessed Mail Order Food."

07:07.830 --> 07:11.000
<b>Blessed Mail Order</b>

07:08.920 --> 07:12.380
I'll have to call this the "Blessed Mail Order Food."

07:12.920 --> 07:14.670
Now then, let's tidy up.

07:14.670 --> 07:17.040
W-wait! I want that.

07:17.380 --> 07:19.580
Uh, this? Why?

07:20.420 --> 07:23.710
Glass jam jars are sparkly and I like them.

07:24.330 --> 07:26.630
This one's also round and it's quite nice, too.

07:26.920 --> 07:29.750
Hmm... It certainly is pretty.

07:31.830 --> 07:35.330
I-I suppose I have no choice but to give you a peek!

07:36.130 --> 07:37.630
Why don't you have a choice?

07:45.630 --> 07:47.460
Ta-da!

07:50.130 --> 07:54.330
L-look! This empty bottle is a hexagon, and it looks cool!

07:54.710 --> 07:56.000
Oh, y-yeah...

07:56.420 --> 08:01.790
<b>Hayashida Co.</b>

07:56.710 --> 07:59.420
And this empty bottle is a pretty color, right?!

07:59.460 --> 08:01.670
Uh, yeah... it sure does.

08:02.040 --> 08:05.380
And this bottle? Well, it looks like some kinda animal!

08:05.380 --> 08:07.330
W-wow...

08:07.500 --> 08:09.750
Why are you so disinterested?!

08:09.880 --> 08:11.830
Huh?! You're angry with me?!

08:12.500 --> 08:19.580
I mean, that is quite the collection,
but... have you always liked them? Those empty bottles?

08:19.580 --> 08:20.580
Y-yeah.

08:21.290 --> 08:25.380
The glassware sourced abroad that I saw
back in the Edo days had a huge impact on me.

08:22.420 --> 08:25.540
<b>Wow!</b>

08:22.420 --> 08:25.540
<b>So sparkly!</b>

08:25.540 --> 08:32.250
<b>SOURCED ABROAD</b>

08:25.710 --> 08:26.880
Sourced abroad?

08:27.290 --> 08:32.130
They were goods brought in from foreign countries.
It was like an Edo period mail order.

08:32.750 --> 08:35.580
Even among the imported goods,

08:35.750 --> 08:38.380
the super prime contents were rare animals
and strange birds from abroad.

08:38.380 --> 08:42.290
Camels and parakeets,
and even elephants and such came to Japan.

08:42.630 --> 08:45.210
Elephants?! Edo had elephants?

08:45.580 --> 08:50.000
Yes. The elephants walked
from Nagasaki Port and came to Edo.

08:50.250 --> 08:53.670
Wow, the people who saw that must have been shocked.

08:54.380 --> 08:57.790
Edo was in the midst
of an unprecedented elephant boom.

08:58.080 --> 09:05.040
Various storybooks and dice games and even
sword guards were made with elephant print patterns.

09:05.040 --> 09:07.080
Awesome, it was a popular mascot.

09:07.080 --> 09:15.420
<b>I must</b>

09:07.080 --> 09:15.420
<b>collect them all...</b>

09:07.090 --> 09:15.420
<b>I-I must</b>

09:07.090 --> 09:15.420
<b>collect them...</b>

09:07.540 --> 09:12.290
I also bought all of the related goods I could
get my hands on. I got an advance on my offerings...

09:12.580 --> 09:14.830
You haven't matured a bit in 400 years?

09:15.460 --> 09:21.080
Well, no matter the time,
Blessed Mail Orders have drawn people's interest.

09:21.210 --> 09:22.670
Even now, here we are...

09:23.460 --> 09:28.130
There's something epic about unusual things
you can't get in your own neighborhood.

09:28.290 --> 09:31.290
Yeah. Honestly, I want to eat one more...

09:32.040 --> 09:33.880
That one's for Koyuzu.

09:34.040 --> 09:37.330
I know that, I'm just admiring it.

09:42.540 --> 09:44.790
Hm? What's wrong, Elda?

09:46.580 --> 09:51.500
Actually... there's another
Blessed Mail Order I received yesterday.

09:52.000 --> 09:52.830
Oh, yeah?

09:55.580 --> 09:57.790
It's a Blessed Basque Cheesecake!

09:57.790 --> 09:58.960
Oh yeah!

09:58.960 --> 10:00.920
Gah, this is good!

10:01.170 --> 10:04.330
The crusty part is slightly bitter,
and it goes super well with cream cheese!

10:08.460 --> 10:11.080
W-we can have this apple pie, too.

10:11.080 --> 10:12.830
Let's split it, come on!

10:12.830 --> 10:15.830
N-no, we won't be halving this...

10:16.080 --> 10:17.500
Are we having one each?!

10:18.040 --> 10:19.630
Let's do this!

10:26.630 --> 10:29.250
Now I'm in the mood for something salty...

10:29.500 --> 10:31.080
Ah, in that case...

10:35.170 --> 10:44.000
<b>Downtown Tokyo Monja Flavor</b>

10:35.210 --> 10:39.500
Ta-da! Exclusive Downtown Tokyo
potato chips, monja flavor!

10:39.920 --> 10:44.290
Eeek! I was just thinking
that a sauce flavor would be perfect! Here!

10:44.210 --> 10:49.250
<b>Mt. Fuji Cider</b>

10:44.210 --> 10:49.250
<b>Izu New</b>

10:44.210 --> 10:49.250
<b>Summer Cider</b>

10:44.540 --> 10:46.540
That sauce flavor makes you crave a fizzy drink, huh?

10:46.710 --> 10:49.460
We've got locale-limited fizzy drinks, yay!

10:49.580 --> 10:52.170
There's ice cream that you bought me earlier, too!

10:52.250 --> 10:55.380
Speaking of, there should be
Nagasaki castela cakes in the shrine office!

11:03.210 --> 11:04.500
This is the best ever!

11:04.670 --> 11:08.540
Let's buy even more Blessed Mail Orders, Koito!

11:08.710 --> 11:11.380
Sounds good! Let's keep ordering!

11:11.670 --> 11:13.210
Here's to our Blessed Mail Orders...

11:13.210 --> 11:15.330
Cheers!

11:16.250 --> 11:22.920
And so the elf and the miko fell completely under
the sweet magical spell of the Blessed Mail Order,

11:23.130 --> 11:24.920
and they indulged in gluttony.

11:29.000 --> 11:33.960
They did not need dinner,
and Koyuzu was quietly angry with them.

11:33.960 --> 11:35.290
Urp...

11:36.540 --> 11:39.500
Sis? Elda-sama?

11:41.080 --> 11:44.210
Er, yeah. Sorry...

11:44.960 --> 11:47.630
I-I am so terribly sorry...

11:58.290 --> 12:02.580
Tsukishima, Chuo Ward, Tokyo, 2 am.

12:18.920 --> 12:20.630
Oh, it's almost time.

12:25.630 --> 12:29.420
I remember the day Sayoko became a miko...

12:35.380 --> 12:41.670
I, Koito Koganei, will have
my miko succession ceremony today.

12:42.670 --> 12:46.380
It will be with Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto, Elda.

12:48.920 --> 12:55.170
S-s-s-so cold! It's scary out there!
I want to go home and play games under the kotatsu!

12:55.290 --> 12:58.960
I knew something was off! Why are you wearing that?

12:58.960 --> 13:00.630
B-because...

13:00.630 --> 13:04.580
I told you that today is a very important ceremony
so dress properly, right?

13:06.290 --> 13:10.380
S-s-s-so cold! I'm gonna die!
I'm immortal but my heart's done for!

13:10.500 --> 13:13.790
My ears! They're cold as ice!

13:13.880 --> 13:20.830
<b>Kinoshita Shop</b>

13:14.210 --> 13:17.790
Thanks Kinoshita-san! I appreciate you
hanging onto Elda's clothes for us!

13:18.000 --> 13:20.080
Not a problem! Good luck with the ceremony!

13:20.830 --> 13:26.790
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

13:21.460 --> 13:25.920
Daughters of the Takamimi Shrine
assume the role of miko upon turning 16.

13:27.130 --> 13:28.830
That year, on the night of the Winter solstice,

13:29.080 --> 13:32.540
the succession ritual is to go around Tsukishima
together with the Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto,

13:32.710 --> 13:36.330
and officially introduce ourselves to the parishioners.

13:37.580 --> 13:41.420
But can't the parishioners come outside
to see us since this is my debut?

13:41.920 --> 13:46.080
I don't think I can handle
meeting so many people at once.

13:46.420 --> 13:48.880
Don't give your bad self analysis so calmly.

13:49.210 --> 13:56.750
Anyway, we can tell all the parishioners that I've officially
become your miko today, so it's an important ceremony!

13:56.750 --> 13:58.170
Don't slack off!

13:59.500 --> 14:00.880
I know that, Koito.

14:02.710 --> 14:06.420
This succession ritual is also something
important to me personally.

14:07.790 --> 14:10.170
So I'm determined to see it through no matter what!

14:10.460 --> 14:14.040
Huh? O-oh, okay. Sorry for doubting you.

14:15.210 --> 14:21.630
I can feel how serious she is.
Normally she's a real pain about rituals and stuff.

14:22.630 --> 14:25.500
Um, then let's get started, Elda.

14:25.670 --> 14:30.040
Right. Just like during a festival,
we'll go in order starting with the first street.

14:35.460 --> 14:38.420
Wow, it's super dark!

14:39.170 --> 14:43.380
Was I wrong to tell the parishioners
that all the lights must be out during the ritual?

14:43.880 --> 14:47.540
Will the parishioners hate me?
Even though it's late at night...

14:47.830 --> 14:52.420
This seems like a lot of fun to me.
Koma-chan said it's exciting to be in the darkness.

14:52.420 --> 14:55.420
We're deliberately staying up all night, you know?

14:55.580 --> 14:58.460
I-I see... then that's good.

14:59.880 --> 15:04.210
We'll go where these paper lanterns
are lit and go around Tsukishima.

15:04.880 --> 15:06.130
Let's head out, Elda!

15:06.380 --> 15:10.460
W-watch your step.
It's dark and it's difficult to see the ste-

15:13.580 --> 15:16.170
Jeez, what are you doing, El-?!

15:18.880 --> 15:20.710
L-let's be careful.

15:21.170 --> 15:23.500
Yeah... let's do that.

15:27.380 --> 15:30.380
So this is how dark it gets when the city lights are out.

15:30.500 --> 15:35.210
I-in the Edo days it was much darker.
We had nothing but the moonlight.

15:35.960 --> 15:38.420
We couldn't even go out at night.

15:38.750 --> 15:43.040
Oh yeah? According to the period dramas
they held torches and went out walking often.

15:43.540 --> 15:48.790
In the early days of Edo, candles were luxury items.

15:49.380 --> 15:54.290
Before long came tradesman
blending together fish oil and used wax.

15:54.830 --> 15:59.330
Little by little the amount of people who went out
walking at night holding paper lanterns increased...

16:00.040 --> 16:04.290
But since that brightness would not allow you to see
the face of someone coming from somewhere else,

16:04.540 --> 16:07.080
the paper lanterns would have the family crest
and trade name and the like on them

16:07.080 --> 16:09.670
so you'd immediately know who you encountered.

16:09.710 --> 16:11.040
<b>Konban</b>

16:10.210 --> 16:14.210
The Edo folk are a playful bunch,
so eventually aside from trade names and crests,

16:11.880 --> 16:13.040
<b>Good Evening</b>

16:14.130 --> 16:15.880
<b>Stretching my legs</b>

16:14.130 --> 16:16.710
<b> Going nowhere in particular</b>

16:14.420 --> 16:18.710
writing things like "Good evening"
and "Stretching my legs” became popular.

16:17.960 --> 16:18.960
<b>GOOD EVENING</b>

16:17.960 --> 16:18.960
<b>STRETCHING MY LEGS</b>

16:20.250 --> 16:24.130
So they were sending messages with their
paper lanterns. What did you write in yours, Elda?

16:24.420 --> 16:29.250
<b>DON'T MIND ME</b>

16:24.750 --> 16:25.960
"Don't mind me."

16:26.500 --> 16:28.330
Seriously, try harder to meet people halfway!

16:56.330 --> 16:59.210
Hear that, Elda? They're singing!

16:59.210 --> 17:00.460
Y-yeah...

17:01.380 --> 17:06.080
Did they sing for the succession ritual
for the last generation's miko?

17:06.380 --> 17:12.000
Yeah, my mom told me about it, too.
They're singing praises of your eternal life.

17:13.250 --> 17:16.380
I actually have some complex feelings about that...

17:16.630 --> 17:18.080
Eh? Why?

17:18.920 --> 17:26.830
Immortality is a natural thing to me.
It's kind of like being praised for toddling around.

17:27.750 --> 17:31.540
If they have to do this, then I want them
to sing about my vast knowledge of manga,

17:31.880 --> 17:33.920
or how great I am at games or something.

17:34.130 --> 17:37.540
If I had my way, I'd make lyrics
about how you're just a slacker.

18:08.420 --> 18:11.000
You okay, Elda? Are you cold?

18:11.210 --> 18:12.790
I-I'm fine.

18:13.250 --> 18:16.080
We're done with the third street
so we've only got a little more left!

18:16.080 --> 18:18.580
R-right, I'll hang in there.

18:19.380 --> 18:22.250
It looks like she's really trying.

18:23.500 --> 18:26.920
She normally hates being outside this much.

18:27.710 --> 18:30.330
Is she trying because I'm becoming a miko?

18:31.880 --> 18:33.290
I'm a little happy about that...

18:35.250 --> 18:41.250
I have to do my best to take the place
of my mother and my ancestors!

18:51.880 --> 18:54.460
Huh? The only lights on are the ones over there.

18:58.790 --> 19:03.500
Koito! Elda-sama! Congrats for reaching the goal!

19:03.710 --> 19:07.580
Koyuzu! It was so cold! And so dark!

19:07.580 --> 19:09.130
Koyuzu? Why are you here?

19:09.290 --> 19:12.500
You did great, Elda-sama. Come on in.

19:12.500 --> 19:13.670
O-okay!

19:13.790 --> 19:16.830
Huh? Wha? What's going on?!
Our goal is the convenience store?!

19:17.250 --> 19:19.540
You mean, Grandpa didn't tell you?

19:20.040 --> 19:23.710
The succession ritual started
when Elda-sama wanted to eat soba

19:23.710 --> 19:26.960
from a night vendor and made trouble
for the first generation miko...

19:27.420 --> 19:30.670
I want it! I want it! I want to eat soba from a night vendor!

19:27.670 --> 19:30.880
<b>I want it! I want it!</b>

19:27.670 --> 19:30.880
<b>I want to eat soba</b>

19:27.670 --> 19:30.880
<b>from a night vendor!</b>

19:31.420 --> 19:37.670
Letting Elda eat ramen in the middle of the night
turned into the miko's entrance exam.

19:43.750 --> 19:48.790
Everyone really does spoil Elda way too much!

19:54.170 --> 19:58.380
Koito, Koito! What're you doing?
Let's eat cup ramen! Come on!

19:59.750 --> 20:01.830
She's suddenly in much better spirits...

20:11.580 --> 20:14.540
<b>Super Bucket Cup</b>

20:24.130 --> 20:25.540
Okay, let's eat!

20:39.080 --> 20:42.290
Eating cup ramen on a cold night really hits the spot!

20:43.330 --> 20:44.170
So toasty!

20:46.880 --> 20:49.580
Oh dang it. It really is good.

20:50.540 --> 20:57.080
It's especially good when you're walking around
in the cold! Working hard at the ritual was worth it!

21:07.170 --> 21:10.080
You're eating the same cup ramen as Sayoko, Koito.

21:10.330 --> 21:11.170
Huh?

21:11.750 --> 21:13.080
Same as my mom?

21:18.250 --> 21:18.880
Yeah.

21:24.920 --> 21:25.750
That's neat...

21:28.000 --> 21:35.420
There are so many things coming to mind that I want to
ask about Ieyasu Tokugawa and my mom and stuff, but...

21:46.170 --> 21:47.790
So toasty!

21:49.580 --> 21:53.000
Something's really comfy about this moment...

21:54.420 --> 21:57.080
I'll save it for later.

23:29.000 --> 23:31.960
<b>Osaka</b>

23:41.750 --> 23:45.080
I have arrived, Hiromimi-sama.

23:47.540 --> 23:50.380
Then let's get a move on... straight to Tokyo!

23:54.330 --> 23:57.210
We're comin', Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto...

23:58.630 --> 24:00.210
No, Elda!

24:03.790 --> 24:08.380
Say, Himawari. You reckon givin' 'em pork buns
from 551 is a decent souvenir?

24:08.670 --> 24:10.580
551 is a plumb perfect gift.

24:10.580 --> 24:14.630
Really? Ya sure? We got the swiss rolls, too, yeah?

24:14.790 --> 24:17.130
Y'all gettin' in, Miss?

24:17.420 --> 24:20.500
Yes, yes we are. Take us to Shin-Osaka.

24:20.500 --> 24:22.790
Can't wait for Tokyo!
